    <UnitTestResult executionId="e4432ab2-9aa8-487e-b1e2-b3146559c4b9" testId="adc246cd-39c8-b151-5f60-3c6299be6df8" testName="ShineMusic.Tests.Acceptance.PlaylistBatchScaleTests.Preview_import_and_enqueue_match_the_retained_legacy_reference_with_chunk_bounded_sql(size: 50)" computerName="暖树" duration="00:00:01.0589340" startTime="2026-11-25T17:27:33.4303608+08:00" endTime="2026-11-25T17:27:34.4890279+08:00" testType="13cdc9d9-ddb5-4fa4-a97d-d965ccfc6d4b" outcome="Passed" testListId="8c84fa94-04c1-424b-9868-57a2d4851a1d" relativeResultsDirectory="e4432ab2-9aa8-487e-b1e2-b3146559c4b9">
      <Output>
        <StdOut>SQLite synthetic size=50, published matches=25, unmatched=25; one observation per workflow after matching warmup.&#xD;
Legacy reference is the pre-batch per-input matcher and import/enqueue loops retained below in test code, not a second execution of removed production code.&#xD;
Both variants read the same synthetic catalog; the extra playlists/queue rows they create do not participate in catalog matching. No source provider search is enabled.&#xD;
preview: legacy SQL=100 (SELECT=100, INSERT=0, UPDATE=0, DELETE=0), totalMs=97.037, transactionMs=N/A; batch SQL=3 (SELECT=3, INSERT=0, UPDATE=0, DELETE=0), totalMs=4.152, transactionMs=N/A&#xD;
import: legacy SQL=176 (SELECT=125, INSERT=51, UPDATE=0, DELETE=0), totalMs=49.369, transactionMs=49.328; batch SQL=6 (SELECT=3, INSERT=3, UPDATE=0, DELETE=0), totalMs=12.208, transactionMs=12.110&#xD;
enqueue: legacy SQL=101 (SELECT=100, INSERT=1, UPDATE=0, DELETE=0), totalMs=119.173, transactionMs=N/A; batch SQL=4 (SELECT=3, INSERT=1, UPDATE=0, DELETE=0), totalMs=13.971, transactionMs=7.819&#xD;
settlement: legacy SQL=201 (SELECT=126, INSERT=25, UPDATE=25, DELETE=25), totalMs=473.886, transactionMs=N/A; batch SQL=32 (SELECT=4, INSERT=1, UPDATE=2, DELETE=25), totalMs=69.290, transactionMs=N/A&#xD;
Settlement baseline is restricted to this seeded scenario: half of completed tasks reference a published import, half reference pending_review; its retained test loop reads each task/import and writes each link/delete/status individually. It is not a reproduction of every old settlement branch. The batch implementation intentionally retains one fenced DELETE per promoted row.&#xD;
Transaction milliseconds are available only when measured around BeginTranAsync through successful CommitTranAsync (legacy test stopwatch / production structured diagnostic). N/A means no separate accurate observation; legacy enqueue used one bulk command without an explicit service transaction.&#xD;
Total times include AOP instrumentation and local SQLite I/O. These single samples do not establish PostgreSQL latency, network effects, P95, concurrency behavior or an acceleration multiple. No timing threshold is asserted.</StdOut>
      </Output>
    </UnitTestResult>
